## NOTE ON THE NEW --stop-file PATH (read, not assumed)
The installer derives --stop-file from -RepoRoot, so the new task's stop file is under the NEW pin
(...wk-harvest-runner-pin-1c69fa35a3\.runtime\harvest-cycle\STOP), NOT the old one. The old stop file
could therefore not have ended the new runner at once, which is the hazard C-g names. C-g's delete was
performed regardless, because the order requires it and it leaves no stale marker behind.
